    {
      "id": "for-each-thread-stack-back-trace",
      "name": "ForEachThreadStackBackTrace",
      "category": "ThreadManager",
      "signature": "ForEachThreadStackBackTrace(Target, Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FThreadManager*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Func",
          "type": "TFunctionRef<bool ( uint32 ThreadId,TCHAR* ThreadName,TConstArrayView<uint64>& StackTrace )>"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Enumerates through all thread stack backtraces and calls the provided function for each one.\nThe callback must return true to continue enumerating, or return false to stop early.\nThis function is primarily intended to iterate over stack traces in a crashing context and\navoids allocation of additional memory. It does not, therefore, perform any safety checks to\nensure that the list of threads is not modified mid-iteration or that the callback does not\nitself allocate memory.\nSimilarly, the thread name and stack trace array memory are only valid for the duration of the\ncallback's execution and must be copied elsewhere if they are to be used beyond its scope."
    },
